node_modules/
.web/package-lock.json
dist/
.web/dist/
# Unminified CPU-profiling artifact (bun run build:web:profile). Build output,
# never committed; listed explicitly because it is a sibling of dist/ and the
# `dist/` rule does not match it.
web/dist-profile/
.env
.env.local
*.db
*.db-journal
data/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
# Anchored to the repo root. A bare `logs/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, and the only directories it was actually hiding were the test
# suites: tests/unit/logs, tests/integration/logs and tests/e2e/logs. Seven
# real tests ran in CI while being invisible to `git add`, so they were never
# committed and never reviewed. No runtime or build step writes a `logs/`
# directory - the app's /api/logs route is code, not a directory - and `*.log`
# above already covers log files, so the root-only rule is all that is needed.
/logs/
.bun/
.cottontail-tmp/
.hutch/
artifacts/
build/
electrobun.config.ts
hutch.config.ts
probe-abort.js
start.bat
/workspace/
web/vite.config.js
web/vite.config.d.ts
# Compiled twins that a bare `tsc` used to emit beside every source file. The
# root tsconfig now sets `noEmit`, so they should never reappear — this is the
# guard against one being committed by accident (13 stale `*.test.js` twins had
# accumulated and were being collected as duplicate test suites).
# `scripts/*.mjs` are hand-written and deliberately NOT matched.
src/**/*.js
scripts/**/*.js
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/binaries/
src-tauri/icons/
dev.out
dev.err

# Scratch artifacts from throwaway harnesses and test runs. These are
# regenerable, carry no information, and are easy to create by accident: a
# verification run that points DATA_DIR at a relative path silently builds its
# whole database inside the repo root instead of a temp directory, one
# `tmp-cri-<pid>/` per run. 11 of them had accumulated here untracked, each
# containing a stray `chat/` tree.
tmp-cri-*/
data-verify-tmp*/

# ── Test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ONE entry for everything the suites write at runtime: the Playwright server's
# data dir and workspace (scripts/start-e2e-server.ts), Playwright's own output
# (traces, screenshots, error-context.md), and the HTML report when it is
# enabled. They used to be four scattered entries at the repo root and under
# `web/`, which is where a real project file would have lived.
#
# `tests/.artifacts/` is inside the test tree that owns it and is the only path
# this repo has that is generated-but-never-committed.
#
# Separate from `data/` on purpose: the suite must never read or write the
# maintainer's live database, and these are deleted and recreated on every run.
tests/.artifacts/

# The HTML report still lands at the repo root when a run passes
# `--reporter=html`, which bypasses `outputDir`. Ignored here rather than
# redirected so an ad-hoc report can never be committed.
playwright-report/

# Local agent tooling state, not project source. `.superpowers/` holds per-task
# progress notes for work still in flight; `prompt.txt` is a scratch task brief.
# Neither belongs in history, and both are worth keeping on disk.
.superpowers/
prompt.txt
# Same class, newer tooling: the browser panel writes verification screenshots
# here. They are per-run artifacts with timestamps in their names, so committing
# them would add hundreds of near-duplicate binaries that never match on a
# re-run.
.openchamber/

# Visual QA evidence, not shipped documentation. `docs/tool-ui-atlas.html` is a
# design-review page whose value is in comparing screenshots against mockups, and
# it pulls in ~3.8 MB of JPEGs to do so. This is the same reasoning that took the
# E2E debug PNGs out of history (see ab8b380): a screenshot is evidence for a
# decision already made, and once the decision is in the code and its tests, the
# pixels are dead weight in every future clone. Kept on disk for whoever wants to
# re-read the evidence; not part of the repository.
#
# NOTE (2026-09-30): this rule was right about the images and wrong about the
# page. The JPEGs stay out - they are the 3.8 MB. The HTML was excluded with
# them, and it carries the *prose*: the `done:` / `Open:` lines and the "Not
# looked at yet" list, which is live state about work still to do, not evidence
# for a decision already taken. The consequence was concrete: the one document
# tracking tool-card work was unversioned, so its findings could not be
# reviewed, diffed, or acted on by anyone else, and they rotted on one machine.
#
# So the status prose is versioned in `docs/tool-ui-tracker.md`, which is the
# file that must change in the same commit as a tool-UI change. The atlas stays
# ignored as the visual evidence it is.
docs/tool-ui-atlas/
docs/tool-ui-atlas.html

# Debug screenshots written by the E2E suite belong in Playwright's artifact dir
# (`tests/.artifacts/playwright`, covered above). The old `web/e2e/*.png` rule is
# gone: that directory no longer exists — the suite moved to `tests/e2e/`.

# A screenshot of the Logs settings surface, taken during visual QA and
# committed by an emergency `git add -A` rather than by a decision. Nothing in
# the repository references it, and the rule at `docs/tool-ui-atlas/` already
# records this repo's position: a screenshot is evidence for a decision already
# made, and once the decision is in the code and its tests the pixels are dead
# weight in every clone (same reasoning as ab8b380 for the E2E PNGs).
#
# The ignore rule is REQUIRED, not decorative: `.gitignore` cannot suppress an
# already-tracked path, so without it the next bulk commit re-adds the file.
# Anchored to the repo root so no nested directory of that name is caught.
/logs-viewer.png
